  "query_preview": "..\n\nNext 7 days (Through Monday)...\n\nA jet max moving overhead and weak warm air advection will bring \nisolated showers (15-25%) to north and northeastern areas through\nthe morning hours.\n\nBreezy conditions will spread west to east today ahead of a\nshortwave and associated cold front moving through tonight into\nWednesday. Expect westerly winds of 40 to 55 mph over the western\nfoothills and widespread gusts of 30 to 40 mph over the plains by\nthis afternoon. With warm temperatures into the 80s to near 90,\nthere is some fire danger concern for areas that saw lower\nprecipitation amounts from the recent event. Take care not to\ncause a spark!\n\nAs the wave moves through, there is a 20-60% chance for showers\nand thunderstorms over the north and east this evening through\nWednesday. The Storm Prediction Center has issued a Marginal Risk\n(level 1 of 5) for northeast Montana, including the northeast \ncorner of Fallon county for today, with wind gusts of 60+ mph and\nquarter size hail as the main threats from any severe storms.\nBreezy conditions continue Wendesday, with widespread gusts of 25\nto 40 mph are expected. The strongest winds will be over the far \neast and down along the east side of the Bighorns, where gusts of\n40-50 mph are possible.\n\nThursday and Friday, occasional pieces of energy will continue to\nmove through the upper level northwest flow, allowing isolated \nafternoon/evening showers and thunderstorms to continue (20% or \nless chance). Into the weekend and early next week, southwest \nflow develops over the northern Rockies as upper troughing moves \ninto the West. This would bring better potential for daily \nthunderstorms as shortwaves lift into the region and plains \nmoisture advects into the area.\n\nHighs today will be in the 80s to near 90, into the upper 60s to\nmid 70s Wendesday. Thursday into next week, temperatures will be\nnear normal, with highs in the 70s to low 80s. Archer",
